{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='draft/update4.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nexp = {\n \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"aa497fcd14934325ba2eabe45fefecd1-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"execution_package\\\": \\\"./epaxos\\\",\n \\\"anchors\\\": [\n   {\\\"material_id\\\": \\\"s-decl-recovery\\\", \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1127, \\\"end_line\\\": 1141},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\": \\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\", \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"handlePrepareReply\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1204, \\\"end_line\\\": 1235}\n ],\n \\\"test_names\\\": [\\\"TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoveryValueAdoptionHolderControl\\\"],\n \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-prepare-reply-adopt\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\",\\\"s-makeballot\\\",\\\"s-handle-prepare\\\",\\\"s-exec-recovery-trigger\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\": {\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Discriminating control for the same 5-replica (F=2) harness and the same message schedule as the value-adoption experiment, with one change: the instance (0,0) recovery is driven by replica 2, which holds the accepted command X (PREACCEPTED_EQ with Cmds X at value ballot 0) rather than by a replica that holds only the accepted coordinates. Everything else is unchanged: the conflicting premise at replica 1, the leader's non-equal pre-accept phase, the Accept broadcast at ballot 0 to replicas 2 and 3, and the crash of replicas 1 and 0 after the broadcast.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n   \\\"Same construction, row sizing, crash model and transport boundary as the value-adoption experiment: in-process replicas with the package's own handlers, marshaled RPC structs decoded per delivery, FIFO per link, no delivery to crashed replicas.\\\",\n   \\\"The recovering replica's own self reply carries the real Status (PREACCEPTED_EQ) and Command (X) because it pre-accepted the value; the harness does not supply or alter that state.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\": [\\\"No client path, no state-machine execution, no recovery timer loop, no master/BeTheLeader designation.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\": {\\\"n\\\": 5, \\\"f\\\": 2, \\\"recoverer\\\": 2, \\\"recovery_ballot\\\": 7, \\\"value_ballot\\\": 0}\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"The harness runs the shared scenario function with recoverer = 2: proposal of X at replica 0, non-equal pre-accept reply from replica 1 followed by its failure, Accept at ballot 0 delivered to replicas 2 and 3, failure of replica 0 after the broadcast, then startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) at replica 2 and completion of the quiescent exchange through the target's own handlers.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\": \\\"A recovery must preserve the value that the recovering replica itself holds at its value ballot: if the coordinator's own reply carries a command, the recovery's phase-1 restart proposes that command rather than a NOOP, and the instance completes with that command.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\": \\\"The recovering coordinator's adoption loop and sub-case dispatch (epaxos/epaxos.go:1236-1313) together with startRecoveryForInstance's self reply (epaxos/epaxos.go:1142-1168): the crash pattern is identical to the value-adoption experiment, so only the coordinator's own knowledge of the value differs.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\": [\n  {\\\"alias\\\": \\\"premise-conflict\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"premise_conflicting_command\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"replica\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"cmd_op\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\": \\\"non-equal-preaccept-reply\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"preaccept_reply\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"acceptor\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\": \\\"leader-accepted-before-crash\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"instance_state\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"replica\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 0}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"phase\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"before_crash\\\"}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 3}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"cmd_op\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\": \\\"holder-before-recovery\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"instance_state\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"replica\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"phase\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"before_recovery\\\"}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"cmd_op\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\": \\\"recovery-start\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"recovery_start\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"replica\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"self_has_command\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": true}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"self_status\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"self_vballot\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 7}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"is_leader\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": false}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\": \\\"remote-replies-carry-no-command\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"prepare_reply\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"has_command\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": false}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\": [\n  {\\\"event\\\": \\\"recovery_proposal\\\", \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"replica\\\", \\\"instance_row\\\", \\\"instance_index\\\"], \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"recovery-start\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"cmd_op\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"quorum_reply_command_op\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": -1}],\n   \\\"description\\\": \\\"The recovery driven by the replica that holds X re-proposes X (cmd_op 1) even though no remote reply carries a command; expected to hold, establishing that the value loss in the value-adoption experiment comes from the coordinator lacking the value rather than from the crash pattern.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\": \\\"instance_state\\\", \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"replica\\\", \\\"instance_row\\\", \\\"instance_index\\\"], \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"recovery-start\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"cmd_op\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\": \\\"phase\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"final\\\"}, {\\\"field\\\": \\\"replica\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 2}],\n   \\\"description\\\": \\\"The coordinator that held X still holds X after the recovered proposal ran to quiescence; expected to hold.\\\"}\n ]\n}\nd['experiment']=exp\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update4.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
